## 3. File-by-File Breakdown

### Backend (`/app`)

*   [main.py](file:///home/zavis/Projects/ai-security/AI-Security-/app/main.py)
    The primary backend entrypoint. It initializes the FastAPI app, registers exception handlers, injects CORS rules, starts shared application services (Conversation Manager, Memory Manager, Prompt Builder), and hooks up the route controllers.
*   [config.py](file:///home/zavis/Projects/ai-security/AI-Security-/app/config.py)
    Houses configurations like host names, local database paths, system prompts, LLM model settings, and timeout variables. Having all configuration variables in one location prevents hardcoded parameters from scattering.
*   [routes.py](file:///home/zavis/Projects/ai-security/AI-Security-/app/routes.py)
    Specifies API router endpoints. It listens for `/health` and `/chat` HTTP requests, extracts parameters, coordinates business logic, and outputs validated responses.
*   [schemas.py](file:///home/zavis/Projects/ai-security/AI-Security-/app/schemas.py)
    Uses **Pydantic** to define strict validation schemas for incoming requests and outgoing responses. This ensures that the backend never processes malformed JSON payloads.
*   [conversation.py](file:///home/zavis/Projects/ai-security/AI-Security-/app/conversation.py)
    Manages short-term conversation context. It keeps a rolling list of recent messages (limited to the last 20 messages by default) so the model knows what was discussed previously, and coordinates with the memory system.
*   [database.py](file:///home/zavis/Projects/ai-security/AI-Security-/app/database.py)
    Handles SQLite database connections, automatically creating `memory.db` and checking that tables are initialized when the application launches.
*   [memory_manager.py](file:///home/zavis/Projects/ai-security/AI-Security-/app/memory_manager.py)
    Encapsulates all SQL CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) database operations. It saves long-term memories, queries them, and manages record retrieval.
*   [ollama_client.py](file:///home/zavis/Projects/ai-security/AI-Security-/app/ollama_client.py)
    The client module connecting to the local Ollama LLM. It manages HTTP request handshakes, handles slow models via timeouts, and contains fallback handlers to return a friendly failure message if Ollama is offline.
*   [prompts.py](file:///home/zavis/Projects/ai-security/AI-Security-/app/prompts.py)
    Builds the structured text payload that the LLM processes. It combines the system instructions (defining the agent's persona), recent conversation history, and persistent memories relevant to the user query.
*   [error_handlers.py](file:///home/zavis/Projects/ai-security/AI-Security-/app/error_handlers.py)
    Formats internal errors and validation issues into clean, readable JSON packets.
*   [logging_utils.py](file:///home/zavis/Projects/ai-security/AI-Security-/app/logging_utils.py)
    Configures loggers to write messages to the terminal console and to text files inside the `logs/` folder.
*   [utils.py](file:///home/zavis/Projects/ai-security/AI-Security-/app/utils.py)
    Contains helper utilities like timing functions to log how many seconds an API request took to execute.

