## 5. Walkthrough of a Chat Request

```
[ User types "Hello" & clicks Send ]
                |
                v
[ Frontend React Chat.tsx makes POST request to http://localhost:8000/chat ]
                |
                v
[ FastAPI routes.py receives HTTP request -> parses request.message ("Hello") ]
                |
                v
[ ConversationManager is called to build the message sequence ]
   ├─ Fetch short-term history (last 20 messages)
   └─ Fetch long-term memory records from SQLite via MemoryManager
                |
                v
[ PromptBuilder assembles system instructions + history + memories + user message ]
                |
                v
[ OllamaClient sends the payload to local Ollama server (http://localhost:11434) ]
   ├─ If Ollama responds: return response text
   └─ If Ollama times out/offline: return fallback message ("I'm temporarily unable...")
                |
                v
[ ConversationManager updates short-term history and saves new memory to SQLite if needed ]
                |
                v
[ FastAPI route returns JSON payload {"response": "..."} to frontend ]
                |
                v
[ React state updates -> message bubble rendered on the Chat page ]
```

